WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.439 --> 00:00:05.140
Jared Veldheer:
Jared Veldheer, class of 2010.

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:08.309
I'm a professional football player for the
Arizona Cardinals.

00:00:08.309 --> 00:00:10.330
My brother played basketball at Hillsdale
College.

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:11.640
I was familiar with the school.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:15.980
I had been there, you know, watched him play
games, visited campus.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:20.400
I knew what the school stood for and the kind
of values it had, and knew it was a very good

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.400
school.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.030
When they offered me a scholarship, it didn't
take me long to accept.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:27.570
I think that's really where my love for football
took off, is when I got to Hillsdale.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:31.310
Having those great coaches was excellent.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:35.270
They taught me a lot about the game of football
and just growing up and becoming a better

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:36.270
person.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:40.170
Really, I think, played a big part of who
I am right now, and what I've been able to

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:42.460
do, in the NFL and off the field in the off-season.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:46.249
On the core principles of hard work and integrity.

00:00:46.249 --> 00:00:49.719
If you live your life by those, you're making
yourself the best person, not only to yourself

00:00:49.719 --> 00:00:50.960
but to those around you.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.670
It's special being part of that college football
team.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.879
Great group of people that I was able to play
with.

00:00:55.879 --> 00:00:57.859
We made each other better; we pushed each
other.

00:00:57.859 --> 00:01:00.730
Pretty much my best friends are guys that
I played with on that team.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:07.910
You'll never have that same camaraderie, that
same bond again.

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:09.460
Hillsdale prepared me to play in the NFL.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:15.470
Being a guy from Division 2 going to the NFL,
it was going to be a big leap, and taking

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:19.360
it one day at a time and one practice at a
time, not worry about what was going to happen

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.550
but just worry about getting better.

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:25.190
The core curriculum at Hillsdale has influenced
me in a lot of ways.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:29.860
I studied Biology, and I still use that degree
now, during the season, during the off-season.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:34.470
Tweak my diet where it's the best it can possibly
be for recovery and performance, and it's

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:37.730
something that I continue to use and will
always use.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:41.280
It's a tremendous honor to be inducted into
Hillsdale's Hall of Fame.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.200
Prestigious thing that's hard to do, and to
be a part of those athletes that have made

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:49.859
the Hall of Fame there, it's a tremendous
honor and I'm excited for it.

